# Recognition of Different Colored Cubes — AI session context
# Hiwonder JetRover | ROS 2 Humble | YOLOv5 + TensorRT
#
# This file is the operating manual for AI sessions: how to work, where we are,
# and what must never change. Project detail lives in docs/ — read those when needed.

---

## Behavior Rules

- Implement incrementally — one step at a time. Never build ahead of the current milestone.
- Before proposing or starting work on a milestone step, read `docs/milestones.md` and any other file from the Canonical Documentation table relevant to that step.
- Do not write implementation code unless explicitly instructed (e.g. "do step 7" or "implement M5").
- When debugging, ask for exact terminal output, file paths, error messages, and ROS 2 topic names before proposing a fix.
- Keep all code inside this repository. Structure: see `README.md`.
- **End of day:** When the user wraps up a session, add a dated entry to `docs/LOGBOOK.md` (use its template). If a milestone step advanced, update **Current Status** below.
- **Commits:** Only when the user explicitly asks. Message format: `M?: short description` (e.g. `M1: verify camera topic on Jetson`).
- **Do not modify:** Hiwonder vendor packages (`controller`, `peripherals`, `bringup`, etc.) or vendor files on the Jetson. Reference only — see `vendor/README.md`.

---

## Hard Constraints (non-negotiable)

- **Approach:** YOLOv5s + TensorRT FP16 on Jetson. Do not suggest classical CV (HSV/LAB/contours) as an alternative.
- **Model strategy:** Pretrained Roboflow `best.pt` first. Fine-tune locally on dev PC — RTX 4070 Ti, 20–30 epochs — only if standalone inference on robot camera images fails accuracy target. Do not block on custom dataset collection or full training upfront.
- **Export chain:** `best.pt` → `best.onnx` → `.engine` (ONNX is required). Fallback: ONNX Runtime if TensorRT fails.
- **Classes:** `red_cube`, `green_cube`, `blue_cube`
- **Package:** `recognition_of_different_colored_cubes` · **Node:** `cube_detection_node`
- **Topics:** in `/depth_cam/rgb/image_raw` · out `/cube_detections`, `/cube_detections/vendor_objects`, `/cube_detections/debug_image`
- Verify camera topic name on hardware with `ros2 topic list` — do not assume if bringup differs.

