**Last completed step:** M5 implementation + Jetson smoke (2026-06-28, card `t_15db4d42`). Built the M5 node end-to-end (commit `f571ea1`) + followup fix to embed `geometry_filter` as a package module and correct the numpy-array truthiness check on `msg.k` in the camera_info callback (commit `cf1cf7e`). Wrote 3 new scripts: `scripts/m5_capture_bag.py` (Jetson `ros2 bag record` wrapper), `scripts/m5_analyze_bag.py` (dev-PC bag analyzer), `scripts/m5_offline_replay.py` (parity-check on saved cubes_depth_2026-06-27). Updated `config/params.yaml` with 29 M5 defaults; updated `package.xml` with message_filters/numpy/PIL/torch/torchvision exec_depends; updated `README.md` with the M5 launch sequence + parameter table. Sync'd the new code to the Jetson via rsync, rebuilt (4.54 s exit 0), and confirmed the node boots + engine loads. Wrote `evaluation/m5_live/report.md` (15.8 KB) with the full M5 evidence summary, the blocker description, and the exact launch + bag commands Maher needs to run once the vendor camera is back. No model/vendor/src edits — `models/best.engine` SHA-256 `c64d3e5e277ea42f3f19f0ba733d6ef25f0403ba2496f8191288d3d6829ec3d1` matches M4a, unchanged.

M4c1 supercedes the prior "raise conf to 0.50 or fine-tune on JetRover-room images" recommendation from the M4b card; the geometry filter is the **necessary** part of the M5 pre-ship gate, the fine-tune is the **conditional** part if Phase 1 leaves residual FPs on V3 or on a tight-bbox real cube.

